# Components: prefer existing, extract when reusable

Before writing markup for interactive or repeated UI, **look for an existing component** in `$lib/components` (especially `ui/`). Use it instead of a raw HTML element with one-off classes.

## Order of preference

1. **Existing app component** — e.g. `Button`, `Icon`, `Dialog`, domain compounds under `components/<domain>/`
2. **bits-ui primitive** wrapped in our `ui/` layer — see [`components-bits-ui`](components-bits-ui.mdc)
3. **New reusable component** — only when no fit exists and you judge the UI will be reused (same pattern in 2+ places, shared chrome, or a clear design-system primitive)

```svelte
<!-- ✅ GOOD — use the shared Button -->
<script lang="ts">
	import { Button } from '#lib/components/ui/button/index.js';
	import { Icon } from '#lib/components/ui/icon/index.js';
</script>

<Button type="button" variant="secondary" size="sm" onclick={goBack}>
	<Icon icon="lucide:arrow-left" class="size-4 shrink-0" />
	Go Back
</Button>
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — hand-rolled button when Button already exists -->
<button type="button" class="inline-flex … rounded-full border …" onclick={goBack}>
	…
</button>
```

## When to create a new reusable component

Create one under `components/ui/` (generic) or `components/<domain>/` (domain-specific) when:

- The same control/layout will appear in multiple screens, **or**
- You are about to copy-paste non-trivial markup/styles, **or**
- Accessibility/behavior belongs in one place (focus, keyboard, open state)

Do **not** extract a one-off that is only used once and has no clear second consumer.

## Do not

- Invent a raw `<button>`, `<select>`, dialog, or menu when `ui/` already covers it
- Bypass `Button` / `Icon` / other `ui` primitives with custom Tailwind chrome “just for this screen”
- Duplicate near-identical markup across files instead of extracting a shared component
